ExpressionUUID->"aa904595-6cbb-bc48-a198-38615cc86213"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["One Graph, Three Theories, Three Numbers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d6c95cc1-8b90-3045-9d89-8a35b2f02bef"],

Cell["The exclusivity graph of the KCBS experiment is the 5-cycle:", \
"CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"682ccd63-30f3-614f-a6e4-1d7a167d04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"633ff405-d0a5-7e4c-9f73-e86de5d566b1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pentagon", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CycleGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"VertexLabels", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Name\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"VertexSize", " ", "->", " ", ".15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "200"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n"}]], "Code",\
ExpressionUUID->"db6dee56-ae62-2d4c-ad9f-4832db04664b"],

Cell["\<\
A deterministic hidden-variable theory can make at most an independent set of \
events true at once; quantum mechanics reaches the Lov\[AAcute]sz number by \
semidefinite programming; a theory constrained only by exclusivity reaches \
the fractional packing number. Three theories, three graph invariants:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"818aa2b3-7c5d-4146-bff6-fcb2e01f6fff"],

Cell["\<\
Classical \[Alpha], quantum \[CurlyTheta] (SDP), exclusivity-only \[Alpha]* \
\[LongDash] the strict hierarchy 2 < Sqrt[5] < 5/2:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"0d83358c-dc1d-8f44-b4c0-e237d106973e"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"280d97d6-ac04-0c4e-8085-052f0bb6cfcd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IndependenceNumber", "[", "pentagon", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"LovaszTheta", "[", "pentagon", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FractionalPackingNumber", "[", "pentagon", "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"30947c47-58e4-6e4d-b303-c176bc379a38"],

Cell["\<\
Wolfram's curated graph data supplies the same three values exactly \
\[LongDash] a free oracle for the library:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"252b861d-80f5-894f-b0fb-b7cd336167aa"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"200db51f-533d-c242-bfa3-85481cffcf26"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"GraphData", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Cycle\>\"", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "#"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<IndependenceNumber\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LovaszNumber\>\"", ",",
      " ", "\"\<FractionalChromaticNumber\>\""}], "}"}]}], "\n"}]], "Code",Exp\
ressionUUID->"a07ad4b6-3d6c-2e41-91e4-ef031c3242ac"],

Cell["\<\
The quantum value is physical: five exact pentagram directions, cyclically \
orthogonal, sum to Sqrt[5] on the cone axis:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"ea4702b8-743f-4548-8e54-2766543a59cb"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"22917077-9103-de46-8d01-7bda28688c72"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dirs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KCBSDirections", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dirs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dirs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
        "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "dirs"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"9b6b3257-7a5b-074f-a8ee-\
3b34991071b0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Why Sqrt[5]: Compose Two Copies", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8ca3d8f3-0ed3-c64b-a10c-9b9131b6271f"],

Cell["\<\
Where does the quantum number come from, if not from Hilbert space? Cabello's \
answer (PRL 110, 060402 (2013)): run two independent copies. Events of the \
doubled experiment are exclusive if they are exclusive in either copy (the OR \
product of graphs, native to Wolfram as GraphProduct's \"Conormal\"), and \
probabilities multiply. Consistent Exclusivity demands every clique of the \
doubled graph carry total probability at most 1. The BlackBox filter checks \
all of them.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ba35aeb-fbe5-f240-a9e3-3d5d28687ffc"],

Cell["\<\
The quantum assignment (1/Sqrt[5] per event) passes all 535 maximal cliques \
of two copies \[LongDash] saturating the ten 5-cliques at exactly 1:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"d4f190dc-e7f1-c946-a415-a089f50ae4f2"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ad0708e8-6268-c049-aff4-a681134afaff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
   RowBox[{"pentagon", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
     " ", "N"}]}], "]"}], "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"ddbb27fb-65bb-5f48-\
8966-9351db020e72"],

Cell["\<\
Wright's exclusivity-extremal box (1/2 per event, the \[Alpha]* point) is \
expelled: every 5-clique overflows at exactly 5/4:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"3c463e64-f58d-0c42-9084-f46202fd2ee5"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"35277ac8-c120-a747-ac77-91897914d079"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
   RowBox[{"pentagon", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
  "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"33131d87-cc6f-e242-9af0-cc21c479ffa5"],

Cell["\<\
The mechanism has zero margin: the heptagon box survives two copies exactly \
at the boundary (\[Omega] = 4, load 1) \[LongDash] no activation, reproducing \
arXiv:2411.09773:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"29edd079-a632-e84c-a957-75c4b8aa107c"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8797471f-d0f7-8f4f-ace2-291e8997e0f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"CycleGraph", "[", "7", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
  "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"873f35c3-e978-9149-972a-075858a154a0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Exact Price of Classicality", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6d6afe94-5a9e-8c48-98b9-324be2cd09b5"],

Cell["\<\
How much of a behaviour can a noncontextual model carry? The contextual \
fraction (Abramsky, Barbosa, Mansfield, PRL 119, 050504 (2017)) decomposes an \
empirical model e = NCF \[CenterDot] e_noncontextual + CF \[CenterDot] e' and \
maximizes the noncontextual weight by linear programming over the \
deterministic global assignments. Wolfram's LinearOptimization supports exact \
arithmetic, so the certificate below is an algebraic identity, not a float.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26e512a9-0018-514e-afc9-e3df4a40c2ee"],

Cell["\<\
The 5-cycle scenario; its incidence matrix has rank 1 + 5 + 5 = 11 \
(Abramsky-Brandenburger Prop. 5.7):\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"45bf99ca-4ac5-7640-9b7b-44af31465f06"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ffb50f45-58e6-504a-9a62-40e417ce23e1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scenario", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CycleScenario", "[", "5", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixRank", "[", 
  RowBox[{"scenario", "[", "\"\<Incidence\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",E\
xpressionUUID->"5d178d8e-455b-5a4a-b015-b7c3544f13cc"],

Cell["\<\
Contextual fractions of the three canonical models, in exact arithmetic \
\[LongDash] classical 0, quantum exactly 2 Sqrt[5] - 4, Wright maximal:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"3e647dea-f540-2c46-babc-f960a02ba772"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e01d25f3-69f7-ed41-8eeb-81a84a4688d7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ContextualFraction", "[", 
      RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}], " ",
      "&"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Classical\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->\
"9f6d88f2-74e7-6844-a9ad-de2187d75459"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Local Truths, Global Lies: the Sheaf View", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2ac786b0-a19a-c34a-8f4d-ec2d7354cdba"],

Cell["\<\
Abramsky and Brandenburger (NJP 13, 113036 (2011)) read contextuality as a \
local-to-global failure: each context's distribution is a local section of a \
presheaf, and contextuality is the obstruction to gluing them into one global \
distribution. The three models stratify cleanly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52312a67-9ee2-e240-9ffa-ee69daeaeec6"],

Cell["\<\
Only the classical model extends to a global probability distribution:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"9855beb4-9cf0-1344-95eb-bfae9a286670"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0ecb70b7-d293-e94e-9766-f7830b2c3c93"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"GlobalSectionQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "@", 
       RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Classical\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "}"}]}], "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->\
"c12a0ae4-d526-2e4c-b198-4e44923f8b89"],

Cell["\<\
Possibilistically the quantum model keeps exactly 11 global assignments \
\[LongDash] the Lucas number LucasL[5] \[LongDash] while Wright's box keeps \
none (strong contextuality):\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"55f7e22c-95a1-a74f-bcee-f51cc3f6fc5d"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4b1abf5d-6420-314b-804b-291078a5f46c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PossibilisticSupport", "[", 
     RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "@", 
       RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PossibilisticSupport", "[", 
     RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "@", 
       RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"LucasL", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "}"}], "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID\
->"3594c6bc-13cd-3242-b21c-fb5603af82a8"],

Cell["\<\
A pre-registered negative result, kept for honesty: the cellular-sheaf \
Laplacian of the cover (Hansen-Ghrist, arXiv:1808.01513) was a candidate \
contextuality measure. Its kernel is the 11-dimensional space of \
no-disturbance models \[LongDash] and all three behaviours already live \
there, so the harmonic residual is blind to contextuality. It is a \
no-disturbance projector, nothing more.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ffc71af-c3ed-ef46-ac23-4837e852dded"],

Cell["\<\
The harmonic residual vanishes on classical, quantum, and Wright alike \
\[LongDash] REJECTED as a contextuality measure:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"7fc3f6d0-f951-2e45-84df-9dcd36f77122"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bca1de27-5c11-7c44-91fe-6dbf2eed9894"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"delta", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CycleCoboundary", "[", "5", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"HarmonicResidual", "[", 
     RowBox[{"delta", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"N", "@", 
       RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Classical\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",ExpressionUUID->\
"49ad82fd-2281-2a4c-a0fd-11704732e844"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Geometry Underneath: One Commutator", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6689f5ad-d743-554b-a9b9-b75b45005483"],

Cell["\<\
The canonical realization (Lapkiewicz et al., Nature 474, 490 (2011)) walks a \
single photon through a cascade of two-mode rotations. Each stage generator \
is a matrix logarithm in so(3) \[LongDash] and the four of them rotate about \
only two axes. The full algebra, and with it the quantum resource, appears \
exactly at the first commutator: locally abelian, globally non-abelian.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a77046bd-5b6d-754e-b5b9-84f901ba5f10"],

Cell["The four cascade generators span only a 2-plane of so(3):", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"8366df4c-fca3-1140-92d1-dc5aa86a746d"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"148d61af-dd5b-5d48-b3aa-f59a37649fd6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gens", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CascadeGenerators", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixRank", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"So3Axis", " ", "/@", " ", "gens"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Tolerance", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}]}]}], "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",ExpressionUUID->\
"521ef297-5d4e-b641-a4f4-a161ab6ff1a2"],

Cell["\<\
One commutator step closes the full three-dimensional algebra:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"3f22dbcf-87ab-3844-89c3-0c02f14ed275"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cf491cbd-8fd1-8d4d-a912-a49bebc78723"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DLADimension", "[", "gens", "]"}], "\n"}]], "Code",ExpressionUUID->\
"8c961bd4-addf-4548-9e7d-6efa67ed7fa3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Why Certificates: They Scale", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0dbd85a4-9427-1f45-a9e6-8cb29e69457d"],

Cell["\<\
A mesh of N single-edge-glued pentagons is a toy model of an MBQC resource. \
Its compiled cluster needs a state vector of dimension 2^(5N); the graph \
certificate is one SDP on 3N + 2 vertices. The certificate also sees \
structure the operator route must compute to find: even-N chains pinch the \
quantum gap shut (\[CurlyTheta] = \[Alpha]), odd-N chains reopen it \
\[LongDash] mesh parity controls quantumness.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0cc1b28-0b1f-9a4d-b5aa-06fb6e62d6f1"],

Cell["\<\
Chains of N glued pentagons: linear certificate growth against exponential \
state-vector cost:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"a5d4a711-e82f-864b-aced-693d2c635995"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ac52f06c-35b7-934d-b906-06f41ebee256"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"chainData", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PentagonChain", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"LovaszTheta", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"IndependenceNumber", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", "^", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"5", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"chainData", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<N\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[CurlyTheta] (SDP)\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\[Alpha]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<state-vector dim\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"c5e29c6f-\
647d-a245-8a14-81c070f0325b"],

Cell["\<\
The quantum gap \[CurlyTheta] - \[Alpha] oscillates with chain parity \
\[LongDash] even chains are classical, odd chains quantum:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"392e03cd-a041-9841-a260-ad12f7f240c4"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a4f0efdc-3891-4c41-b5ee-3c0d0c3ae4ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"#", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"#", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "chainData"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<N (pentagon blocks)\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<\[CurlyTheta] - \[Alpha]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", ".02"}], ",", " ", ".28"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
    "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<quantum gap of pentagon chains\>\""}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "380"}]}], "]"}], "\n"}]], "Code",Exp\
ressionUUID->"83b97992-4ee4-d747-9e8a-3326d27c56d6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Verification", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5d8359c8-07a0-ba40-b62d-e07f687cb37b"],

Cell["\<\
House discipline: every claim above, machine-checked in one association. This \
cell must print OK -> True.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfed75c0-5367-6349-85e2-45e621a38b37"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"93f679e5-1e8a-734d-9983-06601e04def7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"EssayVerification", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<hierarchy\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"IndependenceNumber", "[", "pentagon", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        "2"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FractionalPackingNumber", "[", "pentagon", "]"}], " ", "==", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"5", "/", "2"}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"LovaszTheta", "[", "pentagon", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5.", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
        RowBox[{"10", "^", 
         RowBox[{"-", "6"}]}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<oracle\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"GraphData", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Cycle\>\"", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", "\"\<LovaszNumber\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<geometry\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ")"}], "^",
              "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"KCBSDirections", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "0"}]}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<twoCopies\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
         RowBox[{"pentagon", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"N", "[", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", 
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "5"}], 
           "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Passes\>\"", "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", 
       "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
          RowBox[{"pentagon", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
         "[", "\"\<Worst\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"5", "/", "4"}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"CEFilter", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"CycleGraph", "[", "7", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
        "[", "\"\<Passes\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<exactCF\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ContextualFraction", "[", 
          RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
            RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\""}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
           "       ", 
           RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}], 
         " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "5", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "4"}], ")"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<sheafStrata\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"GlobalSectionQ", "[", 
            RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"N", "@", 
              RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
               RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
          " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Classical\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "}"}]}], ")"}], " ", "===", "\n", 
        "     ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"True", ",", " ", "False", ",", " ", "False"}], "}"}]}], " ",
        "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"PossibilisticSupport", "[", 
          RowBox[{"scenario", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"N", "@", 
            RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
             RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
         "[", "\"\<Size\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"LucasL", "[", "5", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<laplacianRejected\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"HarmonicResidual", "[", 
           RowBox[{"delta", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"N", "@", 
             RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", 
              RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ",
          "/@", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<Classical\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Quantum\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Wright\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"#", " ", "<", " ", 
          RowBox[{"10", "^", 
           RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<dla\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"MatrixRank", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"So3Axis", " ", "/@", " ", "gens"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Tolerance", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"10", "^", 
            RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "2"}], " ", "&&",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"DLADimension", "[", "gens", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "3"}]}]}],
      ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<chains\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"chainData", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
              "2.2360680", ",", " ", "4.", ",", " ", "5.1366009", ",", " ", 
               "7.", ",", " ", "8.1014704"}], "}"}], "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "n", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
          RowBox[{"10", "^", 
           RowBox[{"-", "3"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "\n", "|>"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"EssayVerification", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<OK\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Values", "[", "EssayVerification", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}], "\n"}], "Code",ExpressionUUID->"6b9e28fc-8b50-9243-9a51-\
964a53c6f3a9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Concluding Remarks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9e951474-deac-a844-974b-a73c18bae8e5"],

Cell["\<\
One graph carried the whole argument. The pentagon's three invariants delimit \
three theories; two copies of the experiment force the quantum value; a \
linear program prices the resource exactly; the sheaf view says precisely \
which local consistencies fail to globalize; and one commutator marks where \
the classical description ends. Limitations, stated plainly: the SDP values \
are machine-precision (only the LP certificates here are exact); a classical \
computer reproducing these statistics has no evidential force \[LongDash] the \
sampler knows the context, which is exactly what hidden-variable models are \
forbidden; the sheaf Laplacian was rejected by its pre-registered gate test \
and is kept only as a no-disturbance projector; and the two-copy filter \
provably cannot activate n-cycles with n \[GreaterEqual] 7, so these \
certificates bound from above without singling out the quantum set in general \
\[LongDash] that is Cabello's open D1 problem, not a solved one.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"97b04c85-a9df-2e4a-be74-cf7faab38738"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Future Work", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a20b43fa-a53d-dc44-a581-aacc433966f6"],

Cell["\<\
Run the k = 3 activation probe on the heptagon (343-vertex OR cube; probe \
pre-registered in the pipeline, currently disabled) and chart the open cells \
of arXiv:2411.09773.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8fa8c8b5-b7da-974a-bb05-2051a0813caa"],

Cell["\<\
Replace the rejected Laplacian with \[CapitalCCedilla]ech cohomology of the \
support presheaf (Abramsky-Mansfield-Barbosa, arXiv:1502.03097) as the \
sheaf-level measure, on the same CycleScenario datatype.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d7ab8a6c-487e-7e4b-b6fc-7c90228f4eee"],

Cell["\<\
Correlate DLA growth with contextual fraction under composition on pentagon \
meshes \[LongDash] the FEM study design (H1-H5) built on PentagonChain.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5cef5383-d7f0-334f-bf9d-0563942da109"],

Cell["\<\
Run the two-qubit biphoton encoding of the cascade on gate hardware as a \
genuine platform test, using the Wolfram/QuantumFramework paclet for the \
circuit layer.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2e485c8a-64ce-bf43-b072-c96e048e7fee"]
}, Open  ]],

